The [[Karin]] '''Kuruma''' (Japanese: '''車'''; English: '''Car''') is a four-door sedan featured in as part of the [[GTA Online: Heists|Heists]] update.

The car [[Kuruma (3D Universe)|returns]] from the where it assumed the design of a Japanese sedan, albeit slightly larger and less sporty in design.

{{Gallery
|Kuruma-GTAO-SSASA.png|The '''Kuruma''' on [[Southern San Andreas Super Autos]] in the enhanced version of .
|Kuruma-GTAO-RoofBrakeLights.png|The rooftop brake lights on the Kuruma, absent on the armored variant.
}}

, in .|sound=FranklinClinton-GTAOe-Quote-Agency.ogg}}

[[File:F.Clinton&Partner-GTAOe-TheCrew.jpg|thumb|280px|Franklin Clinton in [[2021]], along with [[Lamar Davis]] (left), [[Imani]] (right), and [[Chop]].]]
Having walked away from [[The Big Score (GTA V)|the Union Depository heist]] with somewhere between $9 million and $42 million, Franklin went on to become a legitimate businessman through investments and other plays. Despite [[Tanisha Jackson|Tanisha]] bidding Franklin an amicable goodbye the day before her wedding with [[Jayden]] at the end of ''GTA V'', her relationship with Jayden somehow ended and she reunited with Franklin. Tanisha married Franklin, moved into his home at [[3671 Whispymound Drive]], and started a family with him. As of December [[2021]], the house is now adorned with children's toys and a slide in the backyard, and an ornamental front wall sign reading "The Clintons". By this time, their children have already started going to school.

